{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be","id":1549877,"title":"What generation would u likely be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-06T11:01:09-07:00","id":1549877,"title":"What generation would u likely be?","content":"Just a fun little question on what generation of kindred you would likely be a member of.<br /> <br /> Personally I would probably start off as member of the 11th or 12th generation Malkavian or Ministry. Be honest what generation would you likely to start off before you moved by amarath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T11:46:55-07:00","id":1549878,"title":"","content":"Tbh I have no idea. It would depend on who Embraced me, and that could be literally anyone in the non-Thin Blood Kindred community. I would like to be 7th or 8th generation, maybe even 6th, but the odds are against it.<br /> <br /> For Clan, I would probably be Toreador, but I could also be Tremere, Ventrue, or even a non-Sabbat Tzimisce (did you know their clan name was taken from the last name of a minor Byzantine Emperor born in the Balkan region)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T12:02:40-07:00","id":1549879,"title":"","content":"I would like to be a member of the 8th or 9th generation, but I don't think that the odds are in my favour unless I really impressed someone like Hesha and no I didn't know about that fact about Tziscme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T13:22:00-07:00","id":1549881,"title":"","content":"Would be nice to end in the 7th or even 8th but wouldn't be against the 6th<br /> Chances are slim to none, realistically speaking, but who knows?<br /> Really depends on my future Sire and Clan<br /> <br /> As a Tzimisce I would actually have a very good chance I would ends up and even would thrive as a strong blooded Koldun<br /> Same with a Kiasyd, I think I would be a good Broken Butterfly, one that not only vallue the solitude of the Library but actively would go out to work &quot;on the field&quot;, gather legends, artefacts, books, part time Henry Jones Sr, part time Flynn Carsen<br /> Even could ends up as Molochim Baali<br /> <br /> I would like to think I might be able to impress a Followers of Set? Maybe? Perhaps?<br /> <br /> Also if I would eds up in Yomi I think I could work thing out with my P'o and crawl back to my body to start my career as a Kuei-Jin and would either start my journey on the Howl of the Devil-Tiger Dharma or on the Song of the Shadow<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T19:34:58-07:00","id":1549892,"title":"","content":"13th Generation bottom feeder Nosferatu or possibly Malkavian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T19:35:37-07:00","id":1549893,"title":"","content":"I never considered that I might gain the attention of a Baali from the Celestial faction, but being vulnerable to religious symbols and my presence over time can cause weird things to happen if I stay in one place to long like a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T22:14:03-07:00","id":1549894,"title":"","content":"Now if this was the Dark Ages, I'd probably would be a member of the 9th or 10th generation and still likely would be a member of the Malkavian clan or a Catiff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T14:24:20-07:00","id":1549922,"title":"","content":"Of course, I could end up being of any generation, it just depends on who chooses to embrace me. I could come up with all sorts of different scenarios for how I could have been embraced. Here\u2019s one possibility\u2026<br /> <br /> All of the \u201cWhat Clan are You?\u201d quizzes I have taken say that I should be Tzimisce. So <br /> <br /> A few years ago I went to New York City on vacation. While there, the Eldest senses by presence with Auspex, likely reading my mind and looking into my future to determine that I was a perfect candidate for the embrace.<br /> <br /> He (they/it?) dispatches his Zantosa servants to prepare me for the embrace. Before the embrace, I have an awesome orgy with all of the most lovely Zantosa ladies, then I\u2019m embraced by the Eldest itself and so I will be a 4th generation Tzimisce. <br /> <br /> Hey, that could happen, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T14:41:40-07:00","id":1549923,"title":"","content":"I usually get Malkavian and Ministry clans in most of the clan quizzes with a few times getting Ravnos and Brujah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T21:50:26-07:00","id":1549934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1549922#post1549922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, I could end up being of any generation, it just depends on who chooses to embrace me. I could come up with all sorts of different scenarios for how I could have been embraced. Here\u2019s one possibility\u2026<br /> <br /> All of the \u201cWhat Clan are You?\u201d quizzes I have taken say that I should be Tzimisce. So<br /> <br /> A few years ago I went to New York City on vacation. While there, the Eldest senses by presence with Auspex, likely reading my mind and looking into my future to determine that I was a perfect candidate for the embrace.<br /> <br /> He (they/it?) dispatches his Zantosa servants to prepare me for the embrace. Before the embrace, I have an awesome orgy with all of the most lovely Zantosa ladies, then I\u2019m embraced by the Eldest itself and so I will be a 4th generation Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Hey, that could happen, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't write this to crash your parade but its something which I've been thinking about for some time.<br /> <br /> Becoming a 4th Generation in the modern age seems like a death sentence to me. Anyone who isn't entirely anathema to diablerie, which is most Cainites and including many Elders, would come after you if your Generation became known and you won't have time to develop your potential sufficiently before they're at your door.<br /> <br /> This is something which I think that many people forget about low Generation. Low Generation gives potential for incredible powers but you don't get it at once nor do you grow your power faster than anyone else. It just that most low Generation Cainites have had time across millennia to develop their potential.<br /> <br /> I will grant that the blood pool and blood expediture would favor along with some stuff like Dominate. But in general I wouldn't put my money on a 4th Generation fledgling against a Ancillae, or even seasoned Neonate, who has developed their potential and knows their business. And even less of a chance against an established Elder. All of whom might have diabliere on their minds at the sight of a 4th Generation fledgling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T01:50:45-07:00","id":1549935,"title":"","content":"Deleted because forum ate it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 04-08-2025, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T04:01:44-07:00","id":1549936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1549934#post1549934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't write this to crash your parade but its something which I've been thinking about for some time.<br /> <br /> Becoming a 4th Generation in the modern age seems like a death sentence to me..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is true, from a certian point of view<br /> But from the other?<br /> You are the Children of an Antediluvian, your mere existence proves the ancient monsters not only real but your Sire was active enough to judge you worthy to be a Child<br /> Rumors about Zapatashura's rampage is one thing, that could be downplayed, faked ,etc<br /> But a &quot;living, breathing&quot; 4th gen &quot;fledgeling&quot;? That would make the Camarilla AND the Sabbat colletively shit bricks and hastly start bulding forts out of it because daddy is in town, all bets off, not some dusty relic like Mithras or Ur-Shulgi, Lazarus or Artemis crawled out of their tomb, so the past would haunt the present but a literal blood god decided time to bring some new blood in the fold<br /> That is HUGE<br /> Last time when this happened was when Gratiano and Augustus were Embraced (not counting the Tremere for obvious reasons) and back then the Antediluvians were pretty active, basically a common knowledge they exist some even met them personally<br /> In the modern era?<br /> <br /> I think it would be like the case of <b>Sergei Voshkov</b>, I'm pretty sure he is the younges 5th generation vampire around Embraced in 1991 by Baba Yaga (or used to be until Vasilisa offed him) but in his arguably pretty short afterlife of a decade no one of the sane mind would even dared to touch him because of the shadow of Baba Yaga - okay, not many survived her culling but the rest who became trapped behind the Shadow Courtain knew about the Eyes of the Crone<br /> <br /> In the modern era to be young, a few years old demigod-in-training would be dangerous, that is true, but I think in the meantime would turn the whole kindred society upside down; half of them would try to have you as a snack <i>maybe</i>, but probably not (like how those 4th Gens before you survived to be Elders, they were young once too, freshly embraced with the similar situation as prime snack-candidates for a qucik jump in power) the other half would court you to have favors and hastly secure a cozy position in the new order, because an active Antediluvian who not lurks around but decided okay, lets see these kids would mean changes. Big changes.<br /> We have a bunch of &quot;What if...?&quot; scenarios (and of course Baba Yaga and Mithras are the &quot;living&quot; example how even a 4th could do it), like Artemis awakening, in the Jyhad diary Enoch possible return or even after the death of Zapathasura Hazimel and Chandraputra making peace and basically redrawing the maps and power balance in India<br /> <br /> (Yaay for spam-flag.... I wil l delete the original)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T09:10:40-07:00","id":1549945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1549934#post1549934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't write this to crash your parade but its something which I've been thinking about for some time.<br /> <br /> Becoming a 4th Generation in the modern age seems like a death sentence to me. Anyone who isn't entirely anathema to diablerie, which is most Cainites and including many Elders, would come after you if your Generation became known and you won't have time to develop your potential sufficiently before they're at your door.<br /> <br /> This is something which I think that many people forget about low Generation. Low Generation gives potential for incredible powers but you don't get it at once nor do you grow your power faster than anyone else. It just that most low Generation Cainites have had time across millennia to develop their potential.<br /> <br /> I will grant that the blood pool and blood expediture would favor along with some stuff like Dominate. But in general I wouldn't put my money on a 4th Generation fledgling against a Ancillae, or even seasoned Neonate, who has developed their potential and knows their business. And even less of a chance against an established Elder. All of whom might have diabliere on their minds at the sight of a 4th Generation fledgling.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make an excellent point. Largely, my post about being 4th generation was just being silly, kinda wish fulfillment. Realistically, being embraced as 4th generation would be a nearly certain death sentence for a modern vampire unless my sire kept a close eye on me to protect me from would be diablerists. If the Tzimisce Antediluvian was giving me his personal protection, then I'd probably be safe. Otherwise not.<br /> <br /> That brings up an interesting idea - that it may be the case that generation is deliberately limited to prevent exactly that sort of problem. For example, the Ventrue Prince of a city decides that it would be good to embrace a worthy human candidate. The Prince is 8th generation, so he should do the embrace right? Why have another vampire of higher generation sire that new vampire when the prince can do it? Well, maybe because the Prince doesn't want every childe in the city to be just one generation higher than him. That would attractive too many diablerists.<br /> <br /> We could take that idea open step further. Clan Tremere decides that they want to embace a talented human into the Clan. Clan Tremere is highly organized, such permission likely goes to the very top or nearly so. Etrius himself can perform the embrace himself, so our fledgling Tremere will be 5th generation. Why not have every new Tremere be 5th generation? They could make that happen. Because the Clan's neonates would be under too much danger. They can control embraces enough to keep generation relatively low among the Clan without making them too tempting of targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T10:22:49-07:00","id":1549949,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs would be freaking out big time when they learn that the antideuvlians are actually real. There's that deep grained skepticism amongst them especially if you mentioned the Sabbat crusade to them.<br /> <br /> Also if an antideuvlian did embrace someone in the modern age especially in the last few years. I think that they would safe as someone like Ventrue, Tziscme, Toreador and perhaps Gangrel or Set would keep a close eye on them and mentor them and would take any attacks on them quite personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T10:46:50-07:00","id":1549950,"title":"","content":"It may not become publicly (among vampires) known that there is a 4th generation neonate. Who would know know and how would they know? Surely, there are ways, but I imagine that the majority of vampires who find out would want to keep it to themselves either to keep the benefits for themselves or out of fear of reprisal. If the information was shared, it would be to accomplishes - like a Sabbat pack that shares the information to plan a Diablerie attack. <br /> <br /> Of the information did get out, it would be a rumor that most vampires would likely disbelieve. In fact, many elders would want to suppress that rumor, perhaps while investigating it themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T10:50:12-07:00","id":1549951,"title":"","content":"Quite true as I'm sure that the neonate 4th generation kindred would be told not to disclose such information until he or she was well versed enough in the Disciplines and being a kindred and what it all entails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T06:19:05-07:00","id":1549963,"title":"","content":"Dhampir. Best of both worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T17:02:29-07:00","id":1549984,"title":"","content":"I don't think a 4th Gen Neonate would be found out if they behave properly.<br /> <br /> Our OOC knowledge of the game (rules and setting) make seems that figuring out Generation is easy, but it is actually very hard. And a Neonate is hardly worth the trouble of going through the few means to do so.<br /> <br /> You'll either be &quot;adopted&quot; by someone of far higher Gen and no clue about the truth, or you'll be assumed to be one more high-gen-almost-thin-blood like so many others.<br /> <br /> But other than that, asking yourself your possible Generation is kinda pointless. Vampires Embrace for many reasons, even the elders and Methuselah sometimes do so just for giggles. Asking clan and whatnot is one thing, but Gen, anyone can be of any Generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T22:46:42-07:00","id":1549997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1549984#post1549984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a 4th Gen Neonate would be found out if they behave properly.<br /> <br /> Our OOC knowledge of the game (rules and setting) make seems that figuring out Generation is easy, but it is actually very hard. And a Neonate is hardly worth the trouble of going through the few means to do so.<br /> <br /> You'll either be &quot;adopted&quot; by someone of far higher Gen and no clue about the truth, or you'll be assumed to be one more high-gen-almost-thin-blood like so many others.<br /> <br /> But other than that, asking yourself your possible Generation is kinda pointless. Vampires Embrace for many reasons, even the elders and Methuselah sometimes do so just for giggles. Asking clan and whatnot is one thing, but Gen, anyone can be of any Generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that and due to meta issues related to mechanics and the (overhyped) shine of elder discipline access &amp; etc, it can be sometimes all too easy to forget that neonates in the 10-8th generations can be quite a big deal on their own right for many kindred cities, where all 7+th gen kindred will be among the prince &amp; primogen ranks, if any.<br /> <br /> In my own &quot;table&quot; (actually a Discord channel) inspired partly by Requiem 2e, partly by the &quot;elder generation&quot; fluff, i ended up tweaking the progression per generation, to give everybody a little more bite for the background dots, what along with some other &quot;quality of unlife&quot; tweaks like 7 dots on character creation and turning a number of the less impressive official elder powers into syntheses (aka devotions, amalgams, discipline combos) has been met with general approval by the whole group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T22:58:02-07:00","id":1549998,"title":"","content":"That's a good point Monteparnas. The antideuvlians may not tell there new childer about who they are and might use an alias and keep the truth about themselves a secret for some time until they feel it's the proper time. If the Toreador methsaulth Helena can pretend to be a neonate or the same with Kenminstri of the Setites and fool nearly everyone. Then a member of the 3rd generation should have no trouble doing it.<br /> <br /> Not to mention not every clan makes a big deal about lineages like the Ventrue, Lasombra or Tziscme clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T09:22:18-07:00","id":1550041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1549997#post1549997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... the (overhyped) shine of elder discipline ... and turning a number of the less impressive official elder powers into syntheses (aka devotions, amalgams, discipline combos).</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever it is worth here, the high Discipline powers have already been a topic of discussion in these forums, and most are seriously underwhelming. A greater number of Discipline Combos is a welcome addition (and even the official books did that as Amalgams and optional powers in V5).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1549998#post1549998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then a member of the 3rd generation should have no trouble doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it funny how so many people disregard the possibility that the Antes are simply up and kicking about.<br /> <br /> They can pass for whatever Generation they want to pretend to be, and in the unlikely event of one being found out they're likely to notice and have plenty resources to deal with whomever did it.<br /> <br /> In fact, again, they may be roaming around as 12th Gen or higher and will hardly need to worry about being found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T11:22:59-07:00","id":1550050,"title":"","content":"I do like the Amalgam powers can be used in place of high level Disciplines and can be customized to fit the nature of your Kindred player character.<br /> <br /> In my case I usually make Amalgam powers that are suitable for the Malkavian clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-12-2025, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T12:54:45-07:00","id":1550056,"title":"","content":"I just want to point out that the main perk of being low generation isn't and hasn't been super cool unique disciplines but the massive blood pool and expenditure limit allowed. A 4th generation fledgling is going to be mighty hungry with a max blood pool of <b>50</b> and a spend limit of <b>10</b> BP per turn. This fledgling is going to be just straight up tougher than most ancillea and some elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T14:13:25-07:00","id":1550058,"title":"","content":"I still on the opinion a 4th generation today would not have a harder time to survive than a 4th generation Embraced before her<br /> Gratiano de Veronese was Embraced in 1130 as a Lasombra and survived in the Clan of social darwinists<br /> Augustus Giovanni was Embraced in 1005<br /> They are the latest 4th Generation Embraced by an Antediluvian and both survived and even traveled in an age when it was very difficult and dangerous to get to A to B<br /> For example Augustus as a feldgeling basically had to get back from Erciyes after his Embrace-Ritual to Venice and he not spent decades learning from Cappadocius, he not even bothered to &quot;wake up&quot; just give the order to Japteh and Constancia to welcome his new kid in the block and they were not really keen about the whole idea to begin with - you can imagine how hostile and tense the whole situation could have been.<br /> Gratiano had to swim basically dressed up as a meat in a shark filled pool...<br /> Both survived, both thrived, just like other 4th Generation vampires before them who survived and becamew ancille and elder and beyond.<br /> I firmly belive contrary to popular belief the further you go back in time the harder it was to be a Vampire, the lupine/garou and other supernaturals from demons to ghosts to the Fae were more active and outright hostile (or friendly, depending the area) and your fellow blood gods not always liked to share their toys<br /> In the modern era with plenty of humans, technology and everything the world could offer I think a 4th generation fledgeling would not have any problem to survive and thrive even the Sabbat or other vampires around; a freshly awakened ancient would have harder time to adjust and possibly wouldn't be able to adapt; my grandfather outright refused to learn how to use a smartphone and he not had the ego of a creature who been worshipped as a God. Heck when I was a kid the most advanced vide game was <i>Pong</i> and I simply lack the hand-eye coordination or anything I need manage to be anything else than a casual player in the most basic of MMOs<br /> But at least more or less comfortable in the modern world and not get a heartattack from a gun or a car...<br /> I think - just like every 4th Generation before them - our new 4th generation fledgeling would be sucesfull and would survive her first few decades either in hiding or publicly in a city where her daddy's descendant rules turning the political situation and the world order upside down because at the end of the day Vampires are social creatures and their society is built around boons and favors not raw power unless you are Odin, Matasuntha the Hun or Wepwawet but even Odin while squeezed the Get of Fenris furry balls untill their eyes popped he built a whole society around himself and the Einherjar found the whole notion of the Silence of Blood sily <br /> And by simply existing a 4th generation kid could offer a TONS of favors and boons if she plays her cards right - but again if an Antediluvian decided okay, for some reason you are Worthy of his blood you are already probably halfway there to be sucesfull","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T14:59:17-07:00","id":1550063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1550041#post1550041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For whatever it is worth here, the high Discipline powers have already been a topic of discussion in these forums, and most are seriously underwhelming. A greater number of Discipline Combos is a welcome addition (and even the official books did that as Amalgams and optional powers in V5).</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Homebrewing tweaks and canon revisions of these issues with V20 and V5 in particular have become much more commonplace through the years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1550041#post1550041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it funny how so many people disregard the possibility that the Antes are simply up and kicking about.<br /> <br /> They can pass for whatever Generation they want to pretend to be, and in the unlikely event of one being found out they're likely to notice and have plenty resources to deal with whomever did it.<br /> <br /> In fact, again, they may be roaming around as 12th Gen or higher and will hardly need to worry about being found.</div> </div> </div> </div>So very true.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy already allows for the temporary boosting of one's own blood potency, simulating some of the benefits of certain generations. It stands to reason that experienced blood magicians might discover a variety of tricks to dilute one's potency temporarily, fake weaker vitae or different lineage, among a number of other possible shenanigans. In one particular game i joked with this by making <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lucian_(Gangrel)\" target=\"_blank\">Lucian</a> (always something of a strange fit for a Gangrel) into his more elusive <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lucian_(Antediluvian)\" target=\"_blank\">namesake</a> hiding in plain sight, &quot;pulling a Portia&quot; of sorts, so to speak.<br /> <br /> In fact older vampires falsifying either generation or lineage to at least some degree is a pretty recurring NPC theme in my games in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-11-2025, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T15:11:44-07:00","id":1550080,"title":"","content":"It would be likely that some of the antideuvlians would be still active and doing whatever interested them in their younger nights..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T16:50:53-07:00","id":1550126,"title":"","content":"You can't embrace a lupine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T12:27:15-07:00","id":1550169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1550056#post1550056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to point out that the main perk of being low generation isn't and hasn't been super cool unique disciplines but the massive blood pool and expenditure limit allowed. A 4th generation fledgling is going to be mighty hungry with a max blood pool of <b>50</b> and a spend limit of <b>10</b> BP per turn. This fledgling is going to be just straight up tougher than most ancillea and some elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> First, this fledgling lacks many of the most elaborate uses for this Blood Expenditure, so most of it will be Healing and physical buffs.<br /> <br /> Second, the problem with Blood is that it is still a resources that requires some economic thinking. This fledgling still needs to replenish, but has far less experience doing so and not a lot of contingencies in place to ease the process.<br /> <br /> Third, since feeding is predation, it can't be done both subtly and in large quantities, and increasing quantities means that this vampire will attract ever more attention and cause more problems, for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> A fledgling that frequently uses most of the Blood they have at their disposal will find a swift end for all the trouble they'll cause, Diablerie or no Diablerie. Instead, while the eventual big expense if in a tight spot can happen, the best survival strategy is to be as conservative as possible, so very close to actually behaving as a 13th gen.<br /> <br /> By the way, that was probably true since always, so while in ancient times vampires were more powerful at the get go, their regular Blood expenditure probably didn't change all that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T17:30:31-07:00","id":1550326,"title":"","content":"If I was a low generation kindred of the 5th or 6th generation and it wasn't common knowledge, I would make sure to pretend to be of a much weaker level. I did that with Aberrent or Palladium Books quite frequently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T09:07:36-07:00","id":1550444,"title":"","content":"Well hopefully at least a generation higher than the most common denominator, but not so high a generation that my starting PC is short of points badly needed elsewhere at Character Creation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T02:15:25-08:00","id":1557408,"title":"","content":"Eh, probably 12th or 13th, as it's supposedly the most common in the modern nights. Most likely clans being Nosferatu or Malkavian.<br /> <br /> If I found myself waking up as a Thinblood, I'd leap at the chance to perform Diablerie the very moment I was informed about its existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1549934#post1549934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something which I think that many people forget about low Generation. Low Generation gives potential for incredible powers but you don't get it at once nor do you grow your power faster than anyone else. It just that most low Generation Cainites have had time across millennia to develop their potential.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but another thing to keep in mind is that 5th edition seems to have nerfed Diablerie somewhat. By which I mean you can only reduce your generation by 1 step, as opposed to previous editions where you had the chance of skipping multiple levels.<br /> <br /> Any 4th generation, even a newborn, is a rare and precious opportunity. If you want to reap the benefits of eating one, you need to work your way down by diablerizing them in numerical order.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, if you're following a Path of Enlightenment (let's say Nodhism), you could farm their blood and use it to mass embrace a bunch of neonates, whom you subsequently diablerize to speed run your ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T09:07:34-08:00","id":1558140,"title":"","content":"8th Generation Brujah, embraced by a 7th Gen Elder Idealist who recognizes my passion and powerful heart. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T12:01:12-08:00","id":1558532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1557408#post1557408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, probably 12th or 13th, as it's supposedly the most common in the modern nights. Most likely clans being Nosferatu or Malkavian.<br /> <br /> If I found myself waking up as a Thinblood, I'd leap at the chance to perform Diablerie the very moment I was informed about its existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, i'm guessing around the same too - between 11th to 13th depending on luck, a Thinblood if fortune has questionable feelings about me.<br /> <br /> Clan? I'd guess those with a political or academic/occult bent might find me useful or interesting, so Brujah, Tremere or Ventrue probably, though Malkavian and Toreador are possible too - maybe a Lasombra, Tzimisce or Cappadocian if i somehow bumped into someone or something obscure, though to be honest any clan might be fair for weird personal circunstances or manias of the one embracing me. 50% chance of the sire ending destroyed or diablerized and myself as a very guarded, distant, paranoid and &quot;slow game&quot;-obsessed Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Thin-bloods are peculiar - while they overall lack in raw supernatural power, their weaknesses are also atenuated what CAN be advantageous and then there's the weirdness of 15th gens being able to conceive/carry a mortal (dhampir) child, what i decided to tinker with as springboard for one or two plot threads in my current chronicle. I can see myself going &quot;No, no, wait - let's try to get a better hang of how this gig actually works before making a jump into the whole vampire canibalism train. We don't age, no prob with taking a few decades in the sidelines, as long as we avoid the Gehenna wackos.&quot;, if i found myself as one, that is.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, thin-bloodedness can, if one adds bits of DAV fluff and fuzzy mechanics to the whole, be seen something of a spectrum more than any particular generation and one may find individuals that have been labeled thin-blooded such as Jenna Cross - and in centuries past for some time, Okulos - who are 11th or better generation. I sort of adopted that fuzziness as a feature in my chronicle, might be said)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1557408#post1557408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but another thing to keep in mind is that 5th edition seems to have nerfed Diablerie somewhat. By which I mean you can only reduce your generation by 1 step, as opposed to previous editions where you had the chance of skipping multiple levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The speed growth of multiple generations and gain of part of the consumed's disciplines has always been the realm of NPC/writer fiat, ST arbitration, houserules and fanon.<br /> By RAW, i remember no edition where diablerie would bump generation by more than 1 step. At most a &quot;you as ST can allow more, if you feel it's appropriate for your chronicle&quot; and leave it to personal preference on individual tables.<br /> <br /> (In contrast with how asinine sometimes the writers would get with tables on ghoul power per generation of regnant or the drawbacks/limitations of thin-bloods &amp; dhampirs per generation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1557408#post1557408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any 4th generation, even a newborn, is a rare and precious opportunity. If you want to reap the benefits of eating one, you need to work your way down by diablerizing them in numerical order.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, if you're following a Path of Enlightenment (let's say Nodhism), you could farm their blood and use it to mass embrace a bunch of neonates, whom you subsequently diablerize to speed run your ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy, that reminds me of a certain all-Assamite cell hidden in Vienna from a table back in the '90s. Crazy times and shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-26-2026, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-27T02:29:19-08:00","id":1558547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558532#post1558532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By RAW, i remember no edition where diablerie would bump generation by more than 1 step. At most a &quot;you as ST can allow more, if you feel it's appropriate for your chronicle&quot; and leave it to personal preference on individual tables.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Montgomery &quot;Monty</b>&quot; <b>Coven</b>, canonically been bumped from 11th to 6th after he ate Mithras - and that diableire was incomplete<br /> <br /> But The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, introduces rules for diablerie that lowers the diablerist's generation by more than one, gaining Discipline dots from Disciplines that the victim had higher than the diablerist and how the victim can possess the diablerist.<br /> Its on page 180.<br /> <br /> &quot;If the victim is of a lower Generation than the diablerist, the diablerist automatically lowers her Generation by one.<br /> Additionally, if the victim was two or more Generations lower than the diablerist, the diablerist rolls Stamina once per turn for each additional Generation after the first, until they fail a challenge or run out of rolls (difficulty9).<br /> Each success lowers the diablerist\u2019s Generation by one and permanently grants them all benefits attributed to the Generation achieved.&quot;\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-27T10:08:14-08:00","id":1558551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558547#post1558547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Montgomery &quot;Monty</b>&quot; <b>Coven</b>, canonically been bumped from 11th to 6th after he ate Mithras - and that diableire was incomplete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, what part of &quot;<i>the realm of NPC/writer fiat</i>&quot; did you somehow miss?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558547#post1558547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, introduces rules for diablerie that lowers the diablerist's generation by more than one, gaining Discipline dots from Disciplines that the victim had higher than the diablerist and how the victim can possess the diablerist.<br /> Its on page 180.<br /> <br /> &quot;If the victim is of a lower Generation than the diablerist, the diablerist automatically lowers her Generation by one.<br /> Additionally, if the victim was two or more Generations lower than the diablerist, the diablerist rolls Stamina once per turn for each additional Generation after the first, until they fail a challenge or run out of rolls (difficulty9).<br /> Each success lowers the diablerist\u2019s Generation by one and permanently grants them all benefits attributed to the Generation achieved.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, good to know a book on V20 finally adressed the subject - damn shame it's in a book about a niche Gehenna cult instead of one of a more general aim/subject like a book on the Blood, elders or something else, but it's better than nothing for certain.<br /> <br /> But the fact that you NEED one &quot;blink and you miss it&quot; section/table in a book that is NOT on itself what one might call a logical place to look for info in the subject to actually spot the difference and looks like my overall point, that V5 &quot;nerfed&quot; nothing about diablerie it's treatment actually the norm by RAW for 99,9% of the story of the game, still very much stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-27-2026, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T13:22:10-08:00","id":1558574,"title":"","content":"I have recently been thinking about a character based on a Ravnos, maybe leaning more into my trickster side, a character who manipulates illusion and plays with the nature of reality. As for generation, maybe something a little higher, 11th or 12th to start with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T16:21:16-08:00","id":1558600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558532#post1558532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thin-bloods are peculiar - while they overall lack in raw supernatural power, their weaknesses are also atenuated what CAN be advantageous and then there's the weirdness of 15th gens being able to conceive/carry a mortal (dhampir) child, what i decided to tinker with as springboard for one or two plot threads in my current chronicle. I can see myself going &quot;No, no, wait - let's try to get a better hang of how this gig actually works before making a jump into the whole vampire canibalism train. We don't age, no prob with taking a few decades in the sidelines, as long as we avoid the Gehenna wackos.&quot;, if i found myself as one, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one major, crucial piece of information people seem to be overlooking with regards to Thinbloods, is that the fancy 'advantages' they have over true vampires are included in the <b>Merits</b> section. Meaning that those kinds of benefits are not even guaranteed to manifest; and if they do, you're never going to get the full package.<br /> <br /> So there is a very real possibility that you could end up as the Reverse Daywalker, where you have all the weaknesses of being a vampire, and none of its strengths.<br /> <br /> Which would royally suck, and not in the good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T02:01:18-08:00","id":1558613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558600#post1558600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one major, crucial piece of information people seem to be overlooking with regards to Thinbloods, is that the fancy 'advantages' they have over true vampires are included in the <b>Merits</b> section. Meaning that those kinds of benefits are not even guaranteed to manifest; and if they do, you're never going to get the full package.<br /> <br /> So there is a very real possibility that you could end up as the Reverse Daywalker, where you have all the weaknesses of being a vampire, and none of its strengths.<br /> <br /> Which would royally suck, and not in the good way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends somewhat on if your reference material for them comes from Revised, V20 or V5, if memory tricks me not.<br /> <br /> All of that said, do the pros &amp; cons balance themselves out in some way for them? Hell, no - <b><i>at best</i></b>, thin-bloods have atenuated versions of the weaknesses common to most kindred, while at the same time losing many of the features one might desire in being a vampire, no denying. Damn, i every time someone brings up the word Daywalker in a context of Thin-Blooded, i can't top giggling at the idea that someone out there might consider &quot;i'll become Blade, kicking @$$ &amp; taking names&quot; as a viable path for them to play even half seriously.<br /> <br /> BUT, it's not always about being the best person or the better equiped to win a race, but the last one standing and crossing the line while everybody else crashed out. Sometimes, it's about being low-maintenance enough to wait out the crapstorm and then grow &amp; thrive in the ensuing vacuum when things even out somewhat again.<br /> <br /> From a narrative perspective at least - to be clear, any and all thin-bloods in my table are NPCs serving a number of niche narrative (and crypto lore-building, since playing occult archeologist-detective is the main schtick of at least one of the PCs and all of them to some degree) roles for the chronicle. In no way setting up Thin-bloods to be big players in the rat race or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-03-2026, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T04:00:20-08:00","id":1558616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558613#post1558613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends somewhat on if your reference material for them comes from Revised, V20 or V5, if memory tricks me not.<br /> <br /> All of that said, do the pros &amp; cons balance themselves out in some way for them? Hell, no - <b><i>at best</i></b>, thin-bloods have atenuated versions of the weaknesses common to most kindred, while at the same time losing many of the features one might desire in being a vampire, no denying. Damn, i every time someone brings up the word Daywalker in a context of Thin-Blooded, i can't top giggling at the idea that someone out there might consider &quot;i'll become Blade, kicking @$$ &amp; taking names&quot; as a viable path for them to play even half seriously.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who tries that is gonna end up like Copper, reduced to a pile of ashes within 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558613#post1558613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BUT, it's not always about being the best person or the better equiped to win a race, but the last one standing and crossing the line while everybody else crashed out. Sometimes, it's about being low-maintenance enough to wait out the crapstorm and then grow &amp; thrive in the ensuing vacuum when things even out somewhat again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The last one standing is nearly always the elder, who has had centuries to refine their strategy, and wields enough power to solo an entire coterie.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the ambitious young'uns are either dying in droves, or being played like a fiddle because they lack the experience necessary to see through the bullshit their superiors are feeding them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T10:28:43-08:00","id":1558620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558616#post1558616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone who tries that is gonna end up like Copper, reduced to a pile of ashes within 24 hours.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ergo, my giggling at the absurdity of such an association.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558616#post1558616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last one standing is nearly always the elder, who has had centuries to refine their strategy, and wields enough power to solo an entire coterie.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the ambitious young'uns are either dying in droves, or being played like a fiddle because they lack the experience necessary to see through the bullshit their superiors are feeding them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many times, but not always. And many times the elder standing at the end is <b>not </b>the one who thought it wielded enough power to solo an entire coterie - and fate found wanting.<br /> Elders need to watch out to not get fed into their own bullshit and bursting for it.<br /> <br /> And sometimes none of that matters because the cosmos spins gears within gears and throws a monkeywrench just to see what cracks, falls or resettle itself into a different pattern.<br /> <br /> So, <i>knowing </i>you are in the rock bottom can be a edge of sorts if one is willing to skid on the bullshit to advance farther and more smoothly, at least for a time.<br /> <br /> (But yeah, being thin-blood is crap and it's not a matter of should one get better somehow, but when)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T16:22:46-08:00","id":1558623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558574#post1558574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have recently been thinking about a character based on a Ravnos, maybe leaning more into my trickster side, a character who manipulates illusion and plays with the nature of reality. As for generation, maybe something a little higher, 11th or 12th to start with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that your character works out for your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T14:46:15-07:00","id":1558999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1557408#post1557408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any 4th generation, even a newborn, is a rare and precious opportunity. If you want to reap the benefits of eating one, you need to work your way down by diablerizing them in numerical order.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my approach in the Princes of Darkness mod on CK3.<br /> <br /> Just grab a bunch of vamps, toss them in my dungeon, then cannibalize them until I'm 4th generation.<br /> <br /> After that, it's time to wait for the Antedeluvian hunt event!<br /> <br /> That being said, it seems like 11th generation is the most common in the modern nights. At least if Nightroad is anything to go by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T15:00:03-07:00","id":1559000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1558613#post1558613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BUT, it's not always about being the best person or the better equiped to win a race, but the last one standing and crossing the line while everybody else crashed out. Sometimes, it's about being low-maintenance enough to wait out the crapstorm and then grow &amp; thrive in the ensuing vacuum when things even out somewhat again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of funny that the people running the Camarilla now are a bunch of Ancillae, who only managed to claim their thrones, because the previous occupants were compelled to abdicate them.<br /> <br /> Yet, they still have the gall to act like they're hot shit when dealing with Fledglings.<br /> <br /> Like, my dudes, it's only been 20 years since you were licking boots and kissing rings. Who the hell do you think you are, acting like you're kings of the castle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T23:57:08-07:00","id":1559005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1559000#post1559000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, my dudes, it's only been 20 years since you were licking boots and kissing rings. Who the hell do you think you are, acting like you're kings of the castle?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair this is the most human behavior you can think of<br /> Any &quot;normal&quot; people who became plotican, any small cog in the system who got promoted to a higher position<br /> Literally anyone who God to honest promised, he will remain the same if...<br /> ..and no<br /> The transformation even if not insant only takes a few days, a week top and all become just like their predecessor before them totally forgetting &quot;where they came from&quot;<br /> And of course a healthy dose of Vampiric nature and WoD - they were licking boots and kissing rings and now grabbed the power, it is natural they expect the same from others, especially from those who are below them<br /> <br /> Even without the added curse of Uriel &quot;Caine and his childer to cling to Darkness, drink only blood, eat only ashes, and be frozen at the point of death, cursed so all they touch would crumble into nothing.&quot;<br /> It is part of your curse to see everything and anything to crumble around you, to basically self-sabotage you or the universe will do it in one way or another - even without knowing this curse to cling into power as long as you can, it is really in the human nature to behave like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T16:05:53-07:00","id":1559022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1559000#post1559000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of funny that the people running the Camarilla now are a bunch of Ancillae, who only managed to claim their thrones, because the previous occupants were compelled to abdicate them.<br /> <br /> Yet, they still have the gall to act like they're hot shit when dealing with Fledglings.<br /> <br /> Like, my dudes, it's only been 20 years since you were licking boots and kissing rings. Who the hell do you think you are, acting like you're kings of the castle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entitlement is everywhere and in all flavors, as uppity public workers or the average Karen are there to show quite well in a daily basis.<br /> Though the kindred being nocturnal might be less self-aware i guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not to mention that a lot, like A LOT, of the so-called &quot;elders&quot; in the immense majority of the major domains connected to the Camarilla - &quot;Old World&quot; or not - are NOT like Chicago with its primogen of 5/6 pre-Convention of Thorns relics and more in the &quot;200s to 300s&quot; years of unlife range. And that when not Primogen &amp; princes in the 100-150 years of unlife like Lodin or most of Berlin by Night's two primogens, for example.<br /> <br /> If the Beckoning was played with anything approaching actual consistency in its effects, by lore &amp; canon in most kindred courts it would be barely noticed.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-25-2026, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-24T11:59:08-07:00","id":1560177,"title":"","content":"Of course the generation, as well as the clan, is ultimately not up to the person being embraced.<br /> <br /> But, if I was chosing based on what I would think fits my personality best, I would choose Tremere or Giovanni/Cappadocians/Hecata.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a reseacher and have in general a very scientific approach to life. I can imagine that, if got turned into a vampire and thus got proof of the supernatural existing, I would want to study it and become a master of magical arts of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","name":"Ichneumon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7279_6.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-25T13:10:44-07:00","id":1560214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1559022#post1559022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention that a lot, like A LOT, of the so-called &quot;elders&quot; in the immense majority of the major domains connected to the Camarilla - &quot;Old World&quot; or not - are NOT like Chicago with its primogen of 5/6 pre-Convention of Thorns relics and more in the &quot;200s to 300s&quot; years of unlife range. And that when not Primogen &amp; princes in the 100-150 years of unlife like Lodin or most of Berlin by Night's two primogens, for example.<br /> <br /> If the Beckoning was played with anything approaching actual consistency in its effects, by lore &amp; canon in most kindred courts it would be barely noticed.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If the Princes and Primogens are so (relatively) young, then the people who replaced them must be even more so.<br /> <br /> Went from having leaders who were centuries old, to those who only have roughly 5 decades of a head start on you.<br /> <br /> And at my current age, I've come to realize that 10 years can pass by much quicker than you think.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Plus, that's another thing to consider. These Ancillae are in charge now.<br /> <br /> That means they've retired from active field work.<br /> <br /> That means they likely aren't focused on improving their skills. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 05-25-2026, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-25T14:52:28-07:00","id":1560216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549877-what-generation-would-u-likely-be?p=1560214#post1560214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Plus, that's another thing to consider. These Ancillae are in charge now.<br /> <br /> That means they've retired from active field work.<br /> <br /> That means they likely aren't focused on improving their skills. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At least that will make things more believable when the neonates get the upper hand in combat.<br /> <br /> Seriously, never liked stories where the enemy who's had centuries / millennia to cultivate their fighting skills gets taken out by what is effectively a novice with only a fraction of their experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://fo